// apply_ability_verb_smoke — corpus-level pin for verb-body
// `apply_ability` (companion to apply_ability_smoke.sim, which pins the
// physics-scope path).
//
// Two surfaces are now reachable:
//
//   1. **Physics-scope** — `physics X { ... apply_ability ... }`. Pinned
//      by `assets/sim/apply_ability_smoke.sim`.
//   2. **Verb-body** — `verb X(self, target: Agent) = ... apply_ability
//      ...` (this file). Landed by Agent A's parser change (commit
//      `a20f3f3c`); the verb expander wraps the ApplyAbility into a
//      synthesised `verb_chronicle_<Name>` physics handler, and the
//      standard physics-lowering pipeline carries it through to the
//      dispatcher kernel.
//
// What this exercises that the inline-source tests in
// `crates/dsl_compiler/tests/apply_ability_smoke.rs` don't:
//   - the .sim corpus surface (file IO + full pipeline against a
//     real fixture), so any regression in the verb-body path
//     surfaces in the same place every other corpus test does.
//   - mirror of how `apply_ability_smoke.sim` pins the physics-scope
//     path; symmetric coverage.
//
// **Runtime today.** Lives at `crates/apply_ability_verb_smoke_runtime`
// — wgpu device test that pre-seeds event_ring with synthetic
// ActionSelected records and asserts the dispatcher kernel writes
// chronicle records byte-for-byte against the CPU oracle. Drives the
// dsl_compiler pipeline (parse → resolve → lower → schedule → emit) +
// the dispatcher kernel half of the verb-body path.
//
// **Closed-loop sibling.** `assets/sim/apply_ability_verb_chronicle_consumer.sim`
// combines this verb-body dispatcher with a chronicle consumer rule
// (`on EffectDamageApplied → agents.set_hp`) and proves agent_hp
// decreases per tick on real GPU. That's the structural template for
// task #138 (Wire one duel_abilities verb to apply_ability). This file
// remains the isolated dispatcher-only pin (no consumer, no agent_hp).
//
// The verb's `score 1.0` is constant — argmax over a single verb
// trivially wins, so the verb fires every tick `self.alive` is true.

event Tick { }

entity Hero : Agent { }

scoring {
  Cast = 1.0
}

verb Cast(self) =
  action Cast
  when  self.alive
  apply_ability agents.level(self) by self target self
  score 1.0
